{"ref":"BDB, רִיק","hw":"רִיק","html":"† <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">רִיק</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. </strong><br><strong>Hiph.</strong>  <strong> make empty, empty out (</strong>Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">رَاقَ (ى)</span> <em>pour out, forth</em>, intrans. (of water, blood, etc.); Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">רִיק</span> <em>empty, pour</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܪܳܩ</span> in deriv.; Assyrian <em>rêḳu</em>, <em>empty</em><strong>)</strong>;—Pf. 1 s. <span dir=\"rtl\">הֲרִיקֹ֫תִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:33\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.33\">Lv 26:33</a> <a data-ref=\"Malachi 3:10\" href=\"/Malachi.3.10\">Mal 3:10</a>; 3 pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">הֵרִיקוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 28:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.28.7\">Ez 28:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 30:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.30.11\">30:11</a>; Impf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">יָרִיק</span> <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 1:17\" href=\"/Habakkuk.1.17\">Hb 1:17</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיָּ֫רֶק</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:14\" href=\"/Genesis.14.14\">Gn 14:14</a> (but v. infr.); Imv. ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרֵק</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 35:3\" href=\"/Psalms.35.3\">ψ 35:3</a>; Inf. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרִיק</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 32:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.32.6\">Is 32:6</a>; Pt. pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְרִיקִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 42:35\" href=\"/Genesis.42.35\">Gn 42:35</a> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 4:12\" href=\"/Zechariah.4.12\">Zc 4:12</a>;— <strong>1.</strong>  <em>empty</em> vessels <a data-ref=\"Genesis 42:35\" href=\"/Genesis.42.35\">Gn 42:35</a> (E) <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 48:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.48.12\">Je 48:12</a>; <em>keep empty</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">לְהָרִיק נֶפֶשׁ רָעֵב</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 32:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.32.6\">Is 32:6</a> (i.e. keep hungry). <strong>2.</strong>  <em>pour out</em> or <em>down</em>, rain <a data-ref=\"Malachi 3:10\" href=\"/Malachi.3.10\">Mal 3:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 11:3\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.11.3\">Ec 11:3</a>, oil <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 4:12\" href=\"/Zechariah.4.12\">Zc 4:12</a>. <strong>3.</strong>  <em>empty out</em> (i.e. <em>draw</em>) sword (cf. Assyrian <em>kakkê ittabbaku</em> [pass.], Dl<sup>HWB 699 b</sup>) <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:9\" href=\"/Exodus.15.9\">Ex 15:9</a> (poem), <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:33\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.33\">Lv 26:33</a> (H), <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 5:2\" href=\"/Ezekiel.5.2\">Ez 5:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 5:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.5.12\">12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 12:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.12.14\">12:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 28:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.28.7\">28:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 30:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.30.11\">30:11</a>; prob. also <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 1:17\" href=\"/Habakkuk.1.17\">Hb 1:17</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">חרבו</span> for <span dir=\"rtl\">חרמוֹ</span> Gie We Now); of lance <a data-ref=\"Psalms 35:3\" href=\"/Psalms.35.3\">ψ 35:3</a>; cf. (si vera l.) <span dir=\"rtl\">וירק חניכיו</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:14\" href=\"/Genesis.14.14\">Gn 14:14</a> (R) <em>led forth</em>, < Sam. <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיָּ֫דֶק</span> (Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">דּוּק</span> Aph. <em>look</em>) i.e. <em>mustered</em> 𝔊 cf. Di al., <span dir=\"rtl\">ויפקד</span> Ball.—In <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:43\" href=\"/Psalms.18.43\">ψ 18:43</a> 𝔊 𝔖 Hup-Now Bae read <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲדִקֵּם</span>; so ‖ <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:43\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.43\">2 S 22:43</a> MT; but De Dr < <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲרִיקֵם</span> (v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, דָּקַק\" href=\"/BDB,_דָּקַק\", dir=\"rtl\">דקק</a>).<br><strong>Hoph.</strong>  <em>be emptied out</em> from vessel: Pf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">הוּרַק</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 48:11\" href=\"/Jeremiah.48.11\">Je 48:11</a>; Impf. 2 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">תּוּרַק</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 1:3\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.1.3\">Ct 1:3</a> (al. 3 fs.; of ointment, in sim.); cf. also <a data-ref=\"Amos 6:6\" href=\"/Amos.6.6\">Am 6:6</a>, where Oort <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּרְקֵי</span> for <span dir=\"rtl\">מִזְרְקֵי</span>.","next":"BDB, רֵיק","prev":"BDB, רִיפַת"}